---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumb } from '../data/site';
import { CLAIMS, REVISIONS, LEDGER_VERSION } from '../data/claims';
import '../styles/ledger.css';
const categories = [...new Set(CLAIMS.map(c => c.category))];
---
<Base title="Evidence ledger | Fasolati" description="Inspect Fasolati's selected claims, experimental settings, sources, interpretation limits and editorial revision history." path="/evidence/" schema={[breadcrumb('Evidence ledger', '/evidence/')]}>
  <article class="science-article ledger">
    <header class="science-hero">
      <p class="section-kicker">The evidence ledger / {LEDGER_VERSION}</p>
      <h1>A claim should<br /><span>show its work.</span></h1>
      <p class="science-lede">The finding. The setting.<br />The line we do not cross.</p>
      <p>This is a selected, maintained reading of evidence and design boundaries, not a systematic review or a certification of clinical readiness. Study findings and Fasolati design rules are labeled separately.</p>
      <div class="inline-actions"><a class="btn bs" href="/claims-ledger.json" download>Download claims (JSON)</a><a class="text-link" href="#revision-history">Read the revision history →</a></div>
    </header>

    <section class="ledger-guide" aria-labelledby="ledger-guide-title">
      <h2 id="ledger-guide-title">Read the setting before the conclusion.</h2>
      <p>Mechanism entries retain their cells, animals or tissue setting. Human treatment results retain their population and intervention. Measurement proposals and design boundaries are not efficacy evidence.</p>
      <p class="boundary-note">“Checked” is an editorial source-check date, not a clinical approval, a systematic-review search cutoff or a guarantee that no newer evidence exists. Proposed changes need a named human reviewer before public release.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="claims-title">
      <h2 id="claims-title">Inspect the claims</h2>
      <div class="ledger-controls" id="ledger-controls" hidden>
        <div><label for="claim-search">Search claims, sources or limitations</label><input id="claim-search" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try: injection, HbA1c, missing…" /></div>
        <div><label for="claim-category">Evidence category</label><select id="claim-category"><option value="all">All categories</option>{categories.map(c => <option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></div>
        <button class="btn bs" id="claim-clear" type="button">Clear filters</button>
      </div>
      <p id="claim-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">{CLAIMS.length} of {CLAIMS.length} claims</p>
      <p id="claim-empty" hidden>No matching claims. Clear the filters or use a broader term.</p>
      <div class="claim-list">
        {CLAIMS.map((c, i) => <section class="claim-record" id={`claim-${c.id}`} data-category={c.category} data-search={`${c.title} ${c.setting} ${c.statement} ${c.boundary} ${c.next} ${c.sources.map(s => s.label).join(' ')}`.toLowerCase()}>
          <div class="claim-record-head"><span class="claim-number">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><p class="claim-category">{c.category} · {c.setting}</p><h3><a href={`#claim-${c.id}`}>{c.title}</a></h3></div><span class="claim-date">Checked {c.reviewed}</span></div>
          <p>{c.statement}</p>
          {c.sources.length ? <p class="claim-sources">Published support: {c.sources.map((s, index) => <>{index > 0 && ' · '}<a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.label}</a></>)}</p> : <p class="claim-sources">Fasolati design rule, not a published study finding.</p>}
          <div class="claim-boundary"><span>Interpretation limit</span><p>{c.boundary}</p></div>
          <details><summary>What would justify the next step?</summary><p>{c.next}</p></details>
        </section>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="revision-history" class="ledger-history" aria-labelledby="revision-title">
      <p class="section-kicker">An inspectable record</p>
      <h2 id="revision-title">What changed, and why.</h2>
      <p>These entries summarize wording corrections made in the September 12 quality review and published in the prior release. Before-and-after descriptions below are editorial summaries, not quotations from the papers. This ledger makes those changes easier to inspect.</p>
      {REVISIONS.map(r => <details class="revision" id={r.id}>
        <summary><span>{r.date}</span> {r.title}</summary>
        <dl><dt>Before</dt><dd>{r.before}</dd><dt>After</dt><dd>{r.after}</dd><dt>Why</dt><dd>{r.reason}</dd></dl>
        <p><a href={`#claim-${r.claimId}`}>Open the current claim and its source →</a></p>
      </details>)}
    </section>

    <section class="ledger-update" aria-labelledby="update-title">
      <h2 id="update-title">Follow the record, not a promise.</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/evidence-updates.xml">evidence updates feed (RSS)</a> provides the dated editorial changes in this snapshot. Copy its address into an RSS reader after this release is published. It is not an email subscription, an automated literature monitor or a promise of a publishing cadence.</p>
      <p>Future entries should identify the claim, source, changed wording, reason and human release reviewer. A correction can narrow a claim, not just strengthen it.</p>
      <div class="inline-actions"><a class="btn bs" href="/partner/?intent=evidence-correction#partner-form">Suggest a correction</a><a class="text-link" href="/science/">Read the full science spine →</a></div>
    </section>
  </article>
  <script src="../scripts/claims-ledger.js"></script>
</Base>
